Revision history for Data-HyperLogLog-Shared

0.04      2026-08-05
          - xt/valgrind.t: run the real interpreter, not a wrapper script. Under
            a shim perl (plenv, perlbrew) valgrind traced the shell and never saw
            the XS, so the test passed regardless of what the module did.
          - An interrupted create no longer leaves a file that can never be opened
            again: such a file is re-initialized when it is provably empty and owned
            by us, and is otherwise reported as incomplete rather than just invalid.
          - Add a frozen read-only mode: freeze() seals a file-backed sketch
            immutable; new_readonly() opens it O_RDONLY / PROT_READ and
            queries it lock-free.

0.03      2026-07-22
          - On-disk format change (v1 -> v2): an existing 0.02 file is
            refused; recreate it.
          - Fix a use-after-free in merge(): sv_isobject on the peer argument
            runs get-magic, so a tied argument can destroy this object before
            its handle is used again. Such a call now croaks.
          - Resolve argument magic before capturing the path string.

0.02      2026-07-03
          - Security and robustness hardening; backing files now created mode
            0600 (pass a file-mode argument to new() for cross-user sharing).

0.01      2026-06-25
          - Initial release.
